From: Sid Jain <sid_26@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtual-fs: separate write flushing from explicit synchronization

AsyncWrite::flush drains pending writes; it is not a disk durability contract.
Add data-only and full sync operations without changing existing provider flush
behavior, and forward them through file wrappers and mounted files. Host files
finish pending writes before the checked operating-system sync. Memory files
retain their no-disk behavior.
---
diff --git a/src/arc_box_file.rs b/src/arc_box_file.rs
